course: dictionary
lesson: 1382
title: Capricorn: a star sign, a constellation and a line on the map
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word, Capricorn, can mean three different things. The words around it tell you which meaning fits, so use the context clues.
explain: «The equator, the Tropic of Cancer, the Tropic of Capricorn and the Arctic Circle are lines of latitude.» Here Capricorn is a line on a map. Lines of latitude run around the Earth and show how far north or south a place is.
explain: «In Sydney and other lands south of the Tropic of Capricorn it is the other way round.» The clue is Sydney, a real place, so this Capricorn is on the map, not in the sky.
fact: Capricorn means «goat-horned».
fact: The Tropic of Capricorn is an imaginary line around the Earth, at about 23.4 degrees south of the equator.
fact: Capricornus is a real constellation, a group of stars pictured as a sea-goat.
fact: In astrology, Capricorn is one of twelve star signs, for people born roughly between late December and mid-January. Such a person is «a Capricorn».
fact: Astrology is a belief, not science, so a star sign is not a fact about the stars.
exercise: «In Sydney and other lands south of the Tropic of Capricorn it is the other way round.» What is Capricorn in this sentence? | A group of stars | A star sign | A goat with horns | *A line on the map
exercise: Maya was born on 5 January. Her friend says, «You are a Capricorn.» What kind of Capricorn is this? | A line of latitude on a map | A place in Australia | A real constellation of stars | *A star sign from astrology, which is a belief
exercise: The Tropic of Capricorn lies at about 23.4 degrees ___ of the equator. Choose the right word. | north | *south | east | west
test: What does the name Capricorn mean? | Star-born | Line-maker | Sea-fish | *Goat-horned
test: Which of these is real science, not a belief? | *A constellation, a real group of stars | A horoscope for January babies | Being a Capricorn decides your luck | A sea-goat that swims in the sky
exam: Which place is NOT crossed by the Tropic of Capricorn? | Australia | Brazil | *Canada | Southern Africa
